So, my best game so far.  Actually got to the Quest for the first time,
and actually breezed through it pretty easily.  Cleaned out Fort
Ludios, also my first time there.  Then I headed back up several levels
to where I had my stash, and my altar.  Played with the altar for a
while, got a few artifacts & spellbooks, and reorganised my inventory &
stash, and headed back down.  I'd already cleared out a Big Room level,
and as I was going back through it I decided I could boogie on a couple
magic traps there for the 4 more Power points (I was already max Cha).

Of course the trap starts pumping out monsters & blinding me first, but
that's OK, I've got telepathy & can take the monsters.  One of the
monsters was a cockatrice, but I offed it quick enough.  In the next
round of beasties I was chasing something down, and walked over the
cockatrice corpse - glad I was wearing my gloves!  But then a couple
rounds later by gloves burned, I'd forgotten they weren't fireproof
like the rest of my armor.  I was still holding out for gauntlets of
power or dexterity, and was just using the best gloves I'd found so
far, without bothering to enchant or *proof them.  So after they burned
for that first time, I took them off, so they wouldn't suffer any
further damage - and you can guess what happened next.  A couple rounds
of monsters later I walk over the same cockatrice corpse again, and
started banging my head on my desk... NOOOO WHY DID I DO THAT?!?!
stupid stupid stupid stupid....

Just a couple games ago I'd died that same way.  Let's see if I learn
this time.



